              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for modesty, then the Kannada for self-respect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ನಂಬು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಂಬು — nambu — \"to believe; to trust\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅವನ ಮಾತನ್ನು ಯಾರೂ ನಂಬಲಿಲ್ಲ. avana mātannu yārū nambalilla. Nobody believed what he said."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ನಂಬಿದೆ, nambide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What or whom you believe takes -ಅನ್ನು. The noun is ನಂಬಿಕೆ, trust."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಂಬು (nambu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3600 lists Kannada nambu, \"to trust, believe\", and nambike, \"trust\", beside Tamil nampu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
