        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮನ್ನಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮನ್ನಿಸು — mannisu — \"to forgive; to excuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತಡವಾಗಿ ಬಂದಿದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ ಮನ್ನಿಸಿ ಅಂತ ಅವನು ಕೇಳಿಕೊಂಡನು. taḍavāgi bandiddakke mannisi anta avanu kēḷikoṇḍanu. He asked to be excused for coming late."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮನ್ನಿಸಿದೆ, manniside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite: ಮನ್ನಿಸಿ, excuse me, close to ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಿ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮನ್ನಿಸು (mannisu) is usually traced to Sanskrit mānana, \"honouring, showing respect\" (Monier-Williams), with the verb ending -isu; to pardon someone is to treat them with regard. The path is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
